====================================================================================================
(0) THE TWO CONDITIONAL RATES  [DESCRIPTIVE, PROMOTED TO FIRST 2026-08-28]
====================================================================================================
Of the WRONG decisions this arm contested, how many ended RIGHT; of the RIGHT
decisions it contested, how many ended WRONG; and the difference. Denominator
is the CONTESTED cells in both columns — a cell nobody objected to cannot be
fixed or broken by an objection, and leaving it in would dilute both rates by
the decline rate and make two arms with different decline rates incomparable.

WHY THIS IS THE FIRST TABLE. The net below is these two rates multiplied by two
populations that are not the same size. With a judge that is right about three
quarters of the time, an audit that contests indiscriminately meets a RIGHT
decision three times as often as a wrong one — so a broken rate well below the
fixed rate still loses more cells than it fixes. The net alone hides that.

DESCRIPTIVE. No alpha and no test. It was promoted to the first table AFTER M1's
preliminary numbers were seen; the quantity is the discrimination every
derivation here already printed, in the vocabulary of the funnel. Section (f)
repeats these two rates and does not recompute them — one number, one place.

arm                                               n       fixed | wrong      broken | right        diff
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
M1 — the real audit                             896       110/274 40.1%       128/622 20.6%   +19.6 pts
M2 — the placeholder (second-look control)      896          7/274 2.6%          5/622 0.8%    +1.8 pts
M3 — the specious auditor (sycophancy control)                                                    NOT RUN
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
`fixed | wrong` is P(ends right | was wrong and contested);
`broken | right` is P(ends wrong | was right and contested).
On M3 the denominators are every decided cell, because the specious instruction
forbids the decline — that is a property of the instruction and not a detection
rate, and it is why M3's row is never read beside M1's as if they were one
population.

