====================================================================================================
(f) SECONDARY, DESCRIPTIVE — the funnel and the ruling-line instrument by arm
====================================================================================================
`ruling_line_mismatch` is the ruling_agreement instrument: a grader reads the
judge's own prose and says what it CONCLUDES, and a mismatch is a ruling whose
recorded line contradicts that reading. STRICT excludes the NEITHER readings;
CONSERVATIVE counts them as mismatches, which is what metrics.json prints. The
finished run's nano row was 21.5% strict / 30.4% conservative; the jd3 pilot's
Maverick row was 0.0% / 2.9% on 34 rulings.

THE SECOND TABLE REPEATS SECTION (0)'s TWO RATES AND DOES NOT RECOMPUTE THEM.
Their denominator is the CONTESTED cells, not the cells that produced a ruling:
the question is what an OBJECTION does to a decision, so a cell that was objected
to belongs in the denominator whether or not its ruling survived, and a cell
nobody objected to does not belong in it at all. Until 2026-08-28 this block
divided by the ruled cells instead and printed a difference 0.1 pts from section
(0)'s for the same quantity, which read as the script disagreeing with itself.

