====================================================================================================
(i) THREE GATES — WHAT IF NOT EVERY OBJECTION IS HEARD?  [POST HOC — added after M1 was seen]
====================================================================================================
Every row here was decided on 2026-08-28, AFTER M1's preliminary numbers had
been seen. None of them is in PREREG.md as it was committed; M4 alone has an
amendment written before its first paid call, and even that is reported BESIDE
P1 as an ablation and never as the endpoint. A rule invented after the table is
printed is not a rule, and the only honest thing to do with one is to label it.

UNDER EVERY ROW THE RULING IS UNCHANGED. The after-state is the ruling's outcome
where the gate admitted the objection and the decision's own verdict where it
refused. No ruling is re-made; these are the same rulings counted differently.

They bracket the answer rather than settling it:
  MECHANICAL   no model at all — every quotation verbatim in the document it is
               attributed to. The weakest filter there is, so a LOWER bound.
  M4           gpt-4.1-mini, same class as the judge and a different family,
               asked whether at least one alleged defect is REAL. The only one
               of the three a real process could actually run.
  HAIKU-VALID  count only what the GRADER called valid. The grader is stronger
               than the judge, so this imports a better reader into the
               decision path: an UPPER bound, and not a process.

