  THE HAIKU-VALID BOUND — count only what the grader called valid   [POST HOC — added after M1 was seen]
====================================================================================================
  NOT A PROCESS, and this row must never be quoted as one. The grader is
  `anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5` — stronger than the judge it would be gating —
  so counting only its `valid` objections imports its reading of the record into
  the decision path. That is the confound that stopped the judgment-debate-2
  chain, arriving by a side door. Read it as 'what a gatekeeper as good as Haiku
  would achieve': an UPPER bound. It is the logic of `outputs/leave-to-appeal.py`.

